- Pay an invoice on its Ark address only with long-lived VTXOs
  An invoice paid with an arkoor gives the receiver the payer's VTXOs with
  their expiry. When the wallet's VTXOs that expire more than
  `Config::direct_pay_min_expiry` blocks after the tip cover the amount,
  the wallet pays an invoice that carries an Ark address of its Ark server
  with an arkoor of those VTXOs only. This also applies without
  `Config::lightning_ark_address_hints`, which now only adds the arkoor
  payment with VTXOs of any expiry.
  [#XXXX](https://github.com/SatoshiPortal/scuttle/pull/XXXX)
  - A BIP 321 URI can carry such an invoice in an `ark-lightning`
    parameter. A Lightning wallet cannot pay it, so the URI also carries a
    `lightning` invoice. The wallet makes the `ark-lightning` invoice the
    default payment option only when it can pay it with long-lived VTXOs.
    Otherwise the option has the error `NoDirectArkPayment`.
